{"path":"io/basic_ios/init","title":"std::basic_ios<CharT,Traits>::init","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::basic_ios&lt;CharT,Traits&gt;::</span>init","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/basic_ios/init","section":"io","kind":"page","summary":"Sets the associated stream buffer to sb and initializes the internal state.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">protected</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> init<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf\"><span class=\"kw1683\">std::<span class=\"me2\">basic_streambuf</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>CharT,Traits<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> sb <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Sets the associated stream buffer to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">sb</span></code> and initializes the internal state.\n</p><p>The postconditions are as follows:\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tr>\n<th> Element\n</th>\n<th> Value\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td> <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ios/rdbuf\">rdbuf()</a></span> </td>\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">sb</span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td> <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ios/tie\">tie()</a></span> </td>\n<td> null pointer\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td> <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ios/rdstate\">rdstate()</a></span> </td>\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">goodbit</span></code> if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">sb</span></code> is not a null pointer, otherwise <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">badbit</span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td> <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ios/exceptions\">exceptions()</a></span> </td>\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">goodbit</span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/flags\"><code>flags()</code></a> </td>\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">skipws <span class=\"sy3\">|</span> dec</span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/width\"><code>width()</code></a> </td>\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/precision\"><code>precision()</code></a> </td>\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"nu0\">6</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td> <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ios/fill\">fill()</a></span> </td>\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">widen<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">' '</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/getloc\"><code>getloc()</code></a> </td>\n<td> a copy of the value returned by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/locale\"><span class=\"kw1911\">std::<span class=\"me2\">locale</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td></tr></table>\n<p>This member function is protected: it is called by the constructors of the derived stream classes <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_istream\">std::basic_istream</a></span> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ostream\">std::basic_ostream</a></span> once the associated stream buffer is known. Until this function is called, every member function (including the destructor) of the default-constructed <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ios\">std::basic_ios</a></span> invokes undefined behavior. Note that <code>basic_ios</code> is a virtual base class, and therefore its constructor is not called by the constructors of those directly derived classes, which is why two-stage initialization is necessary.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td>  sb\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td>  stream buffer to associate to\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div t-dsc-member-nobold-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ios/basic_ios\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>(constructor)</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  constructs the object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"io","title":"Input/output library"},{"path":"io/basic_ios","title":"std::basic_ios"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::basic_ios<CharT,Traits>::init","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Sets the associated stream buffer to sb and initializes the internal state."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"sb"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"(constructor)","note":"constructs the object"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":153,"codeBlockCount":0}
